course: dictionary
lesson: 10388
title: Trespass: going where you should not
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about rules, and trespass is one of them. To trespass is to go onto someone's land or into a building without permission. «Going into someone's garden without asking is rude and is trespassing.» The clue is without asking: you have no right to be there.
explain: Trespass can also be a noun, a trespass, meaning a wrong or sin. You will meet it in an old church prayer: «forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us.» Here trespass means doing wrong, not walking onto land. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: A formal use is different again. To trespass on someone's time or kindness means to take more than you should. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: Trespass means to go onto someone's land or into a building without permission.
fact: In old or church language, a trespass is a wrong, and to trespass means to do wrong.
fact: «Railway lines are deadly»: some rails carry deadly electricity, and people have died going onto the tracks.
fact: Signs such as «No Trespassing» warn you to keep out, and trespassing on railways is illegal.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», the weasels and stoats trespass in Toad Hall and take it over.
exercise: «Going into someone's garden without asking is rude and is trespassing.» What does trespassing mean here? | Waving to the neighbours | *Going onto someone's land without permission | Asking politely to come in | Playing a game in the park
exercise: «A ball over the fence is a small test of manners: you do not climb into the garden, which is trespassing, but knock, say sorry and ask politely.» What should you do if your ball lands in a neighbour's garden? | Climb over quickly and grab it | *Knock, say sorry and ask politely | Leave it there and forget about it | Throw stones at the fence
exercise: In the Lord's Prayer, «forgive us our trespasses» is said. What does trespasses mean in this phrase? | *Wrongs or sins | Pieces of land with paths | Fences around fields | Walks in the countryside
test: The sign says «No Trespassing». What is it telling you? | Walk along the path to the farm | Come in and have a picnic | Ring the bell for help | *Keep out: do not go onto this land without permission
test: «He trespassed on her kindness by asking for a loan every single day.» What does trespassed on her kindness mean? | Gave her a present | *Took more from her than he should | Went into her house without knocking | Made her a cup of tea
exam: «Railway lines are deadly, so trespassing on the tracks is illegal and dangerous.» Why is trespassing on railway lines so dangerous? | The tracks are made of soft grass | *Some rails carry deadly electricity and modern trains are fast and quiet | Trains are slow and noisy, so you can hear them coming | Railways have lovely picnic spots
